<title>USA: Hilton Hotels sells $300 mln five-year notes.</title>
<headline>Hilton Hotels sells $300 mln five-year notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Hilton Hotels Corp was priced on Wednesday, said lead manager Donaldson Lufkin &amp; Jenrette Securities Inc.</p>
<p>The deal was increased to $300 million from an initial size of $200 million.</p>
<p>BORROWER HILTON HOTELS CORP</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON  07.375    MATURITY 06/01/02</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.598  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA1  YIELD   07.473    PAY FREQ SEMI</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P  BBB-PLUS SPREAD  85 BPS/WI CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1675))</p>
